#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/overview.rst:13
msgid "Application Tier"
msgstr "Capa de aplicación"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/overview.rst:14
msgid ""
"The application tier is easily installed with the same apt or yum "
"repository package that |morpheus| is normally distributed with. Advanced"
" configuration allows for the additional tiers to be skipped and leave "
"only the “stateless” services that need run. These stateless services "
"include Nginx and Tomcat.  They can be configured across all regions and "
"placed behind a central load-balancer or geo-based load balancer.  They "
"typically connect to all other tiers as none of the other tiers talk to "
"each other besides through the central application tier. One final piece "
"when it comes to setting up the Application tier is shared storage, which"
" is necessary when it comes to maintaining deployment archives, virtual "
"image catalogs, backups, etc. These can be externalized to an object "
"storage service such as Amazon S3 or Openstack Swiftstack as well. "
"Alternatively, a simple NFS cluster can also be used to handle the shared"
" storage structure.  Alternatively, supported (Platform as a Service) "
"PaaS offerings can be used that provide a NFS compatible shared storage, "
"eliminating the need to manage the underlying infrastructure."
msgstr ""
"The application tier is easily instalado con the mismo apt o yum "
"repository package that |morpheus| is normally distributed with. Advanced"
" configuration allows for the adicional tiers to be skipped y leave solo "
"the “stateless” services that need run. These stateless services include "
"Nginx y Tomcat. They puede configurarse across todos regions y placed "
"behind a central load-balancer o geo-based load balancer. They typically "
"connect to todos otros tiers as none of the otros tiers talk to cada "
"otros besides a través de the central application tier. One final piece "
"when it comes to setting up the Application tier is shared storage, which"
" is necessary when it comes to maintaining deployment archives, virtual "
"image catalogs, backups, etc. These puede ser externalized to an object "
"storage service como Amazon S3 o Openstack Swiftstack as well. "
"Alternatively, a simple NFS cluster can también be used to handle the "
"shared storage structure. Alternatively, soportado (Platform as a "
"Service) PaaS offerings puede usarse that provide a NFS compatible shared"
" storage, eliminating the necesitan manage the underlying infrastructure."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/overview.rst:17
msgid "Transactional Database Tier"
msgstr "Capa de base de datos transaccional"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/overview.rst:18
msgid ""
"The Transactional Database tier consists of a MySQL compatible database. "
"It is recommended that a lockable clustered configuration be used, such "
"as a Galera cluster, which can also provide high availability.  "
"Alternatively, supported PaaS offerings can be used that provide a mySQL "
"compatible database, eliminating the need to manage the underlying "
"infrastructure."
msgstr ""
"The Transactional Database tier consists of a MySQL compatible database. "
"Se recomienda that a lockable clustered configuration be used, como a "
"Galera cluster, which can also provide high availability.  Alternatively,"
" soportado PaaS offerings puede ser used that provide a mySQL compatible "
"database, eliminating the need gestionar the underlying infrastructure."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/overview.rst:21
msgid "Non-Transactional Database Tier"
msgstr "Capa de base de datos no transaccional"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/overview.rst:22
msgid ""
"The Non-Transactional tier consists of an Elasticsearch cluster. Elastic "
"Search is used for log aggregation data and temporal aggregation data "
"(essentially stats, metrics, and logs). This enables for a high write "
"throughput at scale. ElasticSearch is a Clustered database meaning all "
"nodes no matter the region need to be connected to each other over what "
"they call a “Transport” protocol. It is fairly simple to get setup as all"
" nodes are identical. It is also a java based system and does require a "
"sizable chunk of memory for larger data sets.  Alternatively, supported "
"PaaS offerings can be used that provide an Elasticsearch compatible "
"deployment, eliminating the need to manage the underlying infrastructure."
msgstr ""
"The Non-Transactional tier consists of an Elasticsearch cluster. Elastic "
"Search is used for log aggregation data y temporal aggregation data "
"(essentially stats, metrics, y logs). This enables for a high write "
"throughput at scale. ElasticSearch is a Clustered database meaning all "
"nodes no matter the region necesitan ser connected to each other over "
"when lay call a “Transport” protocol. It is fairly simple to get setup as"
" all nodes are identical. It is también a java based system y does "
"require a sizable chunk of memory for larger data sets. Alternatively, "
"supported PaaS offerings puede ser used that provide an Elasticsearch "
"compatible deployment, eliminating the need to manage the underlying "
"infrastructure."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/overview.rst:25
msgid "Messaging Tier"
msgstr "Capa de mensajería"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/overview.rst:26
msgid ""
"The Messaging tier is an AMQP based tier along with STOMP Protocol (used "
"for agent communication). The primary model recommended is to use "
"RabbitMQ for queue services. RabbitMQ is also a cluster-based queuing "
"system and needs at least 3 instances for HA configurations. This is due "
"to elections in the failover scenarios RabbitMQ can manage. If doing a "
"cross-region HA RabbitMQ cluster it is recommended to have at least 3 "
"Rabbit queue clusters per region. Typically to handle HA a RabbitMQ "
"cluster should be placed between a load balancer and the front-end "
"application server to handle cross host connections.  Alternatively, "
"supported PaaS offerings can be used that provide a RabbitMQ compatible "
"deployment, eliminating the need to manage the underlying infrastructure."
msgstr ""
"The Messaging tier is an AMQP based tier along con STOMP Protocol (used "
"for agent communication). The primary model recommended is para usar "
"RabbitMQ for queue services. RabbitMQ is también a cluster-based queuing "
"system y needs al menos 3 instances for HA configurations. This is due to"
" elections in the failover scenarios RabbitMQ can manage. If doing a "
"cross-region HA RabbitMQ cluster se recomienda have al menos 3 Rabbit "
"queue clusters per region. Typically to handle HA a RabbitMQ cluster "
"debería ser placed entre a load balancer y the front-end application "
"server to handle cross host connections. Alternatively, soportado PaaS "
"offerings puede usarse that provide a RabbitMQ compatible deployment, "
"eliminating the necesitan manage the underlying infrastructure."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/overview.rst:29
msgid "HA Installation Architectures"
msgstr "HA Installation Architectures"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/overview.rst:31
msgid "3-Node HA (Recommended)"
msgstr "3-Node HA (Recommended)"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/overview.rst:32
msgid ""
"In the current 3-Node HA architecture, the Application, Messaging, and "
"Non-Transactional Database tiers are deployed across the three |morpheus|"
" application nodes. The Transactional Database Tier is not installed on "
"those nodes. Configure all three application nodes to use the same "
"external MySQL cluster or supported MySQL service. This external database"
" is a required part of the 3-Node HA topology, not an optional co-located"
" tier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/overview.rst:34
msgid "Distributed HA"
msgstr "Distributed HA"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/overview.rst:35
msgid ""
"In this architecture, the tiers do not need to reside on the same "
"machines, each can be hosted by a supported cluster or PaaS offering.  "
"This provides flexibility and reuse of already existing technologies such"
" as RabbitMQ or Elasticsearch.  Each tier should be architected to "
"provide HA following the vendor's documentation, to ensure no downtime "
"for the |morpheus| Application Tier."
msgstr ""
"In this architecture, the tiers do not necesita reside on the same "
"machines, each puede ser hosted by a soportado cluster o PaaS offering.  "
"This provides flexibility y reuse of already existente technologies como "
"RabbitMQ o Elasticsearch.  Each tier debería ser architected to provide "
"HA following the vendor's documentation, to ensure no downtime for the "
"|morpheus| Application Tier."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/supported_paas.rst:2
msgid "Supported PaaS Offerings"
msgstr "Supported PaaS Offerings"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/supported_paas.rst:4
msgid ""
"The Morpheus Application Tier can be deployed to any public or private "
"cloud.  Morpheus has underlying technologies that support the Application"
" Tier, which can be automatically installed and embedded on the "
"applications nodes. Alternatively, the services can be provided "
"externally and not be embedded.  Many cloud providers have Platform as a "
"Service (PaaS) offerings of these underlying technologies but some are "
"not native or don't provide the performance required. Below is a list of "
"PaaS offerings that are supported to be used for Morpheus:"
msgstr ""
"The Morpheus Application Tier puede ser deployed to any public o private "
"cloud.  Morpheus has underlying technologies that support the Application"
" Tier, which puede ser automatically installed y embedded on the "
"applications nodes. Alternatively, los servicios puede ser provided "
"externally y no be embedded.  Many cloud providers have Platform as a "
"Service (PaaS) offerings of these underlying technologies pero some are "
"no native o don't provide the performance required. Below is a list of "
"PaaS offerings that son soportados to be used for Morpheus:"

